set_m":[11776,13056,2816,2816],"reduce":2,"bytes_transferred":128942233,"bytes_measured_by":"GDAL network statistics (CPL_VSIL_SHOW_NETWORK_STATS)","srcwin":[74566,121988,11264,11264],"grid_shift_m":[0.007213976234197617,0.07518943800823763],"grid_shift_note":"source pixels taken as they are; +x east, +y north: where the source grid sits relative to the site grid"}},"start":{"name":"Bradbury Landing","lon":137.441633,"lat":-4.589467,"heading_deg":90,"x":3446.9,"z":3194.2},"pois":[{"id":"landing","name":"Bradbury Landing","lon":137.441633,"lat":-4.589467,"note":"Curiosity's touchdown point, 6 August 2012 (UTC).","source":"NASA/JPL MSL waypoints, site 2 drive 0 (sol 3 localisation of the landing site; the rover first drove on sol 16)","x":3446.9,"z":3194.2,"elevation_m":-4501.1},{"id":"yellowknife_bay","name":"Yellowknife Bay, John Klein","lon":137.44913,"lat":-4.589485,"note":"Where Curiosity drilled its first rock, John Klein, on sol 182, and Cumberland on sol 279: mudstone laid down in an ancient lake.","source":"NASA/JPL MSL waypoints, site 6 drive 0 (end-of-drive localisation sol 166; the rover stayed within 2 m of it until sol 295)","x":3889.9,"z":3195.3,"elevation_m":-4520.2},{"id":"darwin","name":"Darwin (Waypoint 1)","lon":137.426291,"lat":-4.607115,"note":"The first science stop on the drive toward Mount Sharp: a conglomerate outcrop studied on sols 390 to 401.","source":"NASA/JPL MSL waypoints, site 16 drive 50 (end-of-drive localisation sol 392)","x":2540.4,"z":4240.3,"elevation_m":-4505.3},{"id":"cooperstown","name":"Cooperstown (Waypoint 2)","lon":137.415,"lat":-4.622334,"note":"A layered outcrop examined with the arm on sols 440 to 453.","source":"NASA/JPL MSL waypoints, site 22 drive 0 (end-of-drive localisation sol 440)","x":1873.2,"z":5142.4,"elevation_m":-4493.6}],"poi_source_url":"https://mars.nasa.gov/mmgis-maps/MSL/Layers/json/MSL_waypoints.json","notes":["There is no separate CTX mosaic pair at this site: every level comes from the two USGS 'MSL Gale Merged' mosaics (DEM 1 m, orthophoto 0.25 m) or their own overviews.","Those mosaics merge HiRISE products with CTX and HRSC products where no HiRISE stereo pair exists, without a per-pixel source flag, so 'measured' here means 'in the published mosaic', and the true resolution away from the HiRISE pairs is coarser than the grid.","The orthophoto grid (origin 8126248, -241164; 0.25 m) is not aligned with the DEM grid: imagery windows take the nearest source pixels (no resampling), a shift of under 8 cm recorded in sources.hirise_ortho.grid_shift_m."],"bytes":57331306,"quality":"MSL Gale merged mosaic (HiRISE, with CTX and HRSC beyond it): 5 m imagery and 4 m terrain everywhere; 0.5 m imagery and 1 m terrain along the traverse"}